PS5 HDMI: no re-arm for the re-announce during a 4K120 link setup (v1.8.9)  [ps5-bazzite-deck]

hsgodd (LG OLED, 4K120 + VRR + HDR, Game Mode <-> desktop): the TV re-announces its EDID ~0.3 s
after our 4K120 setup while it trains the FRL link; the re-arm took that for a TV wake-up and
cycled crtc-0, i.e. a new 4K120 setup, which made it re-announce again: a modeset loop with long
black stretches, during which Game Mode's GPU page faults hit and the TV itself locked up.
Within 10 s of a 4K120 setup, a re-announce no longer re-arms; the 4K120 link check from
v1.8.5 (0x7019) decides whether the setup worked and falls back to 4K otherwise.
